{"content":[{"c":["GUR, Ascent of"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Elevated place near Ibleam where Ahaziah, king of Judah, was smitten by the soldiers of Jehu of the northern kingdom. From Gur, Ahaziah fled to Megiddo, where he died (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.9.27","r":"2Kgs.9.27","rawR":"2Kgs.9.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.9.27","value":"2Kgs.9.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 9:27"},"). Though its location is uncertain, some identify it with the Akkadian Gurra, about one-half mile (800 meters) south of Jenin."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GurAscentof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 9:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.9.27","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.9.27","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.9.27"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f9019769c5d07efb6d06abd852aaf67c7e4ebdf389cfee8cc2fb94f0dc2848be","sourceItemName":"GurAscentof","sourceItemOrder":227,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"GurAscentof","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gur, Ascent of","title":"Gur, Ascent of","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}